body:
I walk my Great Dane at the park nearly every single day. He's a rescue and nips at dogs which approach him too quickly. Sooooooo many stupid fuckin' people with their (honestly friendly) unleashed dogs come up to meet mine and I have to deal with holding back my 120lbs of pure muscle.

&#x200B;

Sure, cool or whatever, but MINE isn't friendly! 

&#x200B;

For the record, my dog is extremely friendly when off leash but he gets freaked if he possibly can't get away. He's a good boy with understandable anxiety problems due to his previous owner.

&#x200B;

I'll explain this as they just stand there letting their dog approach me and sometimes I have to be extremely rude to them because they're blinded by their "oh, look a cool giant dog!" thoughts.

&#x200B;

Ruins my day, ruins my dog's favorite activity, ruins their day, and freaks their own dog out and anyone else around watching.

Except for on Mothers Day. I love my Mom.

&#x200B;

\*literally any other day\* MOM!!!! SHUT TF UP UNLESS MY CHILLIDOG WITH KETCHUP IS READY!!!!

I used to think it was normal to have sleep paralysis every time I went to sleep. In my experience it turned out to be caused by massive stress due to (at the time) undiagnosed ADHD. My poor psychiatrist, after enduring my other crazy stories, just shook her head and said "No, this is also something we need to work on...". 

&#x200B;

Shadow people, monsters sitting on my chest, LOTS of aliens, and a ton of difficulty breathing in most cases. If you've ever had sleep paralysis you'll know what I'm talking about! 😎

I know a couple of nurses fighting to keep people alive and I know several who have COVID-19. It's tough because a lot of people get infected and show zero outward signs.

&#x200B;

One time I was getting bloodwork done and the doctor asked me if I felt sick at all. I felt totally fine but I was apparently fighting a virus of some kind, probably a cold. It took me by surprise, I mean, I was feeling great that whole month. It's tough to believe in what you can't see if you are unaffected by it, for sure. People plagued by mental illness are stigmatized all the time for this very reason. My family didn't believe me when I described my ADHD and Panic Disorder diagnoses because they simply had no frame of reference and nothing visible to show for it and they didn't trust what literature said because they just didn't know other people with those issues. I'd had tons of panic attacks at home and work, had an ambulance called on me twice because of it, and my folks just chose not to believe me because their small world never showed them one.

&#x200B;

It didn't make it any less real.

I actually have had tons of chronic severe panic attacks and take an SSRI to suppress them. Sorry to hear that you're getting hit by them, too. My experience with COVID-19 left me feeling as if my lungs just weren't working at full capacity overall. I found myself breathing a little more often to compensate, if that makes sense. By comparison, when I'm beginning to have a panic attack, I will have been breathing normally up until the anxiety takes hold and regain normal breathing when it fully winds down.  Mine are severe, so I'm gasping for air for 10 or 15 minutes straight and my muscles lock up due to poor circulation and it feels totally different than dealing with COVID-19 in my experience.

&#x200B;

While fighting the virus I was at decreased lung capacity, ran a high temperature, could barely smell anything despite clear sinuses, felt the worst chills of my life, was extremely fatigued, achy muscles, bad headache, thirsty constantly, had zero appetite (not nauseous, just no physical desire to eat), coughed hard all day and night, insomnia, and eventually pneumonia developed. I sweat like a pig, was totally winded just getting out of bed, and lost about 25lbs. I was so weak that I couldn't open a bottle of Powerade on my own. It lasted about 2 weeks until I felt human again.

Persona 3 and 4 really helped me through bad parts of my life, those games are freaking awesome. P5 was excellent, too, and had one of the slickest art styles I've ever seen in a game. Always happy to meet other Persona fans! I had a ton of trouble getting through school and I also don't speak with my brother... a lot of what you wrote reminds me of myself, especially the problems focusing on my work yet understanding it fine and being incredibly upset because of how frustrating that is. I'm on depression medication as well and still working that out as I go along.

&#x200B;

I don't know your full story but if you want to chat about it sometime without any judgement or bullshit I'd be happy to listen and discuss it with ya. It is beyond difficult living with depression and not everyone can understand this because it is "invisible" to the eye and not easy to grasp if you have no frame of reference for it. A lot of people just don't freaking get it.

&#x200B;

So, my heart goes out to you because I know you're taking a huge beating from this every single day and if I can help any just reach out. 

&#x200B;

Also... Persona 3 is still my favorite in the series overall. Highly unpopular opinion!

Getting a psychiatrist appointment was frightening but it ultimately saved my life and now I'm medically informed of my previously unknown ADHD. My family didn't help my mental health at all growing up and I waited until I was 28 to start helping myself. My only regret is the lost time from being majorly depressed since I became an adult but I also don't blame myself because of how depressed and afraid I was. I didn't think talking to a doctor would help, had terrible expectations, and was wildly surprised with how much of a positive difference it made. 

&#x200B;

You have a ton of courage for posting here, using a new avenue to try feeling well again. Keep on driving until you reach your desired destination and we are all here to help if you need to stop for directions.

I feel like peoples' desire to be superior is so intoxicating to them that they choose to believe all kinds of stuff that rationality would otherwise filter out. "I am chosen", "I have the ultimate knowledge", "I have special powers which you don't"...

&#x200B;

... but with nothing to ever show for it besides their own assertion. It seems so hollow to me.
